            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.131,
            0.718,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Regroup 1 Hundredths as 10 Thousandths. 10 Thousandths ÷ 3 3 Thousandths, and 1 Thousandths remain. Regroup 1 Thousandths as 10 TenThousandths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.213,
            0.717,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This never seems to end! Each time we divide by 3, there is a remainder of 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.252,
            0.371,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will this process end?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.735,
            0.137,
            0.84,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.735,
                0.137,
                0.84,
                0.285
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.276,
            0.717,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In long division, we see that at each step we get a remainder of 1. So, the process will never end!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.315,
            0.718,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 10 ÷ 3 cannot be expressed using a finite number of digits in the decimal form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.358,
            0.512,
            0.377
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "10 \\div 3 = 3.333 \\ldots"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.382,
            0.847,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are decimal divisions where the quotient never ends! We will explore such numbers in greater detail in a later class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.431,
            0.641,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you find the quotients of 10 ÷ 9, and 100 ÷ 11?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.699,
            0.436,
            0.888,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7) 1 ( 0.142857142857..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.457,
            0.399,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now divide 1 by 7 (1 ÷ 7)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.481,
            0.294,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will this end?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.505,
            0.684,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note all the remainders we get. It starts with 1, then 3, then 2, then 6, and so on. Let us represent this as a chain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.569,
            0.449,
            0.67
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_18_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array}{l}1 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{1 }} 3 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{2 }} 2 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{3 }} 6 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{4 }} 4 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{5 }} 5 \\\\5 \\xleftarrow{ \\text{3 }} 4 \\xleftarrow{ \\text{4 }} 6 \\xleftarrow{ \\text{1 }} 2 \\xleftarrow{ \\text{2 }} 3 \\xleftarrow{ \\text{1 }} 1 \\\\\\downarrow \\\\1 \\xrightarrow{ \\text{1 }} 3 \\ldots\\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.686,
            0.684,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you observe? Can you explain why this division never ends?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.725,
            0.684,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Not only do the remainders repeat in a cycle, the digits of the quotient also repeat in a cycle! 0.142857 142857 14…"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.806,
            0.453,
            0.829
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Magic Number: 142857"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.833,
            0.685,
            0.874
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider the number 142857 that arose when dividing 1 by 7. Multiply 142857 by numbers from 1 to 6."
            }
          ]
